course: dictionary
lesson: 3658
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word fish is a good example. It can be a noun or a verb. «Other reef animals win by tricks: a fake eye near the tail, a fish that swells into a spiky ball.» Here a fish is an animal that lives in water.
explain: «Jesus fed five thousand people with a boy's five loaves and two fish.» Here fish means the food people eat, not a swimming animal. Ask yourself: could the words fit with eating? Loaves and baskets point to food, so this meaning fits.
explain: Fish can also be a verb, and it means to try to catch fish. To fish for something means to search for it, like fishing in your bag for keys. Put your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
explain: The plural of fish is usually fish: one fish, many fish. Fishes is used for many kinds of fish, such as different kinds of fish in a tank or a river.
fact: Fish is a noun and a verb: a fish swims, and people fish.
fact: «Fish» means an animal that lives and swims in water, breathes with gills and has fins.
fact: «Fish» can also mean the meat of fish that people eat, as in «fish and chips».
fact: To fish means to try to catch fish. To fish for something means to search for it.
fact: The plural of fish is usually «fish», but «fishes» is used for many kinds.
exercise: «Fish can live with an uneven fin from birth or injury.» In this sentence, what is a fish? | *An animal that lives and swims in water | The meat people eat with chips | To try to catch fish from a boat | A pet that needs a bowl and food
exercise: Amir says, «I will fish in my bag for my keys.» What does fish mean here? | *Search for something | Swim fast through the water | Eat a meal of cooked fish | Catch a fish from a river
exercise: The plural of fish is usually what? | fisher | fishes | *fish | fishs
test: What does fish mean in «two fish» in the story about the five loaves? | A fin on a fish | *The meat of fish that people eat | Animals that live in water | To catch fish
test: Which sentence uses fish as a verb? | «Fish and chips is my favourite meal.» | *«We went to fish in the lake all morning.» | «The fish has gills and fins.» | «Fish swim in the river.»
exam: Jade says «fish» always means an animal. What is the best answer? | Yes, fish can only mean the meat people eat | No, fish means to swim very fast | Yes, fish is always an animal and nothing else | *No, fish can also mean the meat people eat, or to try to catch fish
